    "updated_at": "2017-07-11T12:34:05Z",
    "body": "I'm going to move on to range requests & downloads, but in the mean time… any ideas how I could write tests?\r\n\r\nI *think* all browsers will issue ranges requests for a simple wav file that's seeked, which I can automate in browsers that support autoplay. However, the spec doesn't require browsers to make range requests, so it feels like a bad approach. Is there any kind of \"unable to test\" warning I could create in this situation.\r\n\r\nOr, should I make it a manual test, where you have to seek a media element to generate range requests?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/314429144/reactions",
