    "created_at": "2017-07-11T15:41:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-11T15:41:01Z",
    "body": "> I _think_ all browsers will issue ranges requests for a simple wav file that's seeked, which I can automate in browsers that support autoplay. However, the spec doesn't require browsers to make range requests, so it feels like a bad approach. Is there any kind of \"unable to test\" warning I could create in this situation.\r\n\r\nIn general it's OK to write tests that aren't fully required by the spec. This is especially true if all browsers pass them. (Or intend to pass them, e.g. all use range requests.)",
